%% Eraser corridor preview then terminal commit sequence
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber

  actor User as User pointer
  participant Surface as CanvasSurface
  participant Tools as CanvasToolPort
  participant IE as InteractionEngine
  participant Preview as CanvasPreviewState
  participant Frame as FrameEngine
  participant Spatial as SpatialKernel
  participant Geometry as GeometryPolicy
  participant EK as EditKernel
  participant Store as DocumentStoreKernel
  participant Draft as DraftDocument
  participant Touched as TouchedSet
  participant CC as CommitCompiler
  participant Projection as DocumentProjectionCache
  participant Events as EventBuffer
  participant Signals as Public signals

  User->>Surface: pointer down in draw mode with eraser tool
  Surface->>Tools: handlePointer(CanvasPointerSample down)
  Tools->>IE: normalized finite down sample
  IE->>IE: admit one active pointer token
  IE->>IE: read finite eraserThickness and start eraser session
  Note over IE: Session stores pointer token, sessionId, eraserThickness, and corridor points in world coordinates.
  IE->>Preview: publish kind eraser with first corridor point
  Preview->>Frame: request overlay repaint only
  Frame->>Preview: capture overlayRevision and eraser corridor once
  Frame->>Frame: build immutable eraser corridor overlay primitive
  Frame->>Signals: publish overlay repaint request
  Signals-->>Surface: repaint overlay eraser corridor

  loop pointer move samples for same token
    User->>Surface: pointer move
    Surface->>Tools: handlePointer(CanvasPointerSample move)
    Tools->>IE: normalized finite move sample
    IE->>IE: append corridor point and trim if interactive eraser soft limit is exceeded
    Note over IE: Corridor remains preview state only, no selected-move main-scene preview is staged.
    IE->>Spatial: query corridor envelope inflated by eraserThickness / 2 + hitPadding + 4.0
    Spatial-->>IE: committed candidate handles from content hit scope
    IE->>Geometry: exact eraser segment-to-family checks for visible deletable candidates
    Geometry-->>IE: tentative touched ids for session only
    Note over IE,Geometry: Read-only candidate refresh can guide terminal intent, but it does not mutate selection, Store, spatial index, or caches.
    IE->>Preview: replace immutable eraser corridor preview snapshot
    Preview->>Frame: request overlay repaint only
    Frame->>Preview: capture overlayRevision and corridor once
    Frame->>Frame: build immutable eraser corridor overlay primitive
    Frame->>Signals: publish overlay repaint request
    Signals-->>Surface: repaint overlay eraser corridor
  end

  alt stale non-terminal sample or second pointer down during active routing
    Surface->>Tools: handlePointer(CanvasPointerSample move/down)
    Tools->>IE: stale token or unsupported concurrent pointer
    IE-->>Tools: ignore without preview, edit, repaint, or action
  else cancel, mode change, dispose, or invalid terminal cleanup
    User->>Surface: cancel or external interruption
    Surface->>Tools: terminal cleanup request
    Tools->>IE: cleanup active eraser session
    IE->>Preview: clear eraser corridor and active session
    Preview->>Frame: request overlay repaint cleanup
    Frame->>Signals: publish overlay cleanup repaint request
    Signals-->>Surface: repaint overlay without eraser corridor
    Note over EK,Signals: No EditKernel commit, Store mutation, spatial remove, projection eviction, main repaint, or erase action is published.
  else loadDocument success interrupts active eraser
    Surface->>Tools: terminal cleanup request from external load success
    Tools->>IE: cleanup active eraser session
    IE->>Preview: clear eraser corridor and active session
    Preview->>Frame: request overlay repaint cleanup
    Frame->>Frame: defer overlay cleanup to loadDocument post-install repaint scheduling
    Note over EK,Signals: No eraser EditKernel commit, eraser spatial remove, eraser projection eviction, eraser main repaint, or erase action is published.
    Note over Signals: No public eraser repaint signal is published before the successful load install boundary.
    Note over Store,Frame: The loadDocument success Store mutation, spatial rebuild, projection eviction, and main plus overlay repaint are external load effects covered by seq_load_document_success.
  else same-token pointer up
    User->>Surface: pointer up
    Surface->>Tools: handlePointer(CanvasPointerSample up)
    Tools->>IE: same-token finite terminal sample
    IE->>IE: append terminal point if distinct and trim corridor to eraser point limit
    IE->>Spatial: query final corridor envelope for content hit candidates
    Spatial-->>IE: committed candidate handles with generation and structuralRevision
    IE->>Geometry: exact eraser checks, require isDeletable and exclude background elements
    Geometry-->>IE: final erasedElementIds in document order

    alt final erasedElementIds is empty
      IE->>Preview: clear eraser corridor and active session
      Preview->>Frame: request overlay repaint cleanup
      Frame->>Signals: publish overlay cleanup repaint request
      Signals-->>Surface: repaint overlay without eraser corridor
      Note over Touched,Signals: No touched set, revision change, spatial remove, projection eviction, main repaint, public document notification, or erase action is published.
    else at least one element is erased
      IE->>EK: open synchronous interaction edit
      EK->>EK: reject disposed or nested edit
      EK->>Store: read committed revision snapshot
      Store-->>EK: committed tables and revision
      EK->>Draft: create rollback-safe draft
      IE->>Draft: remove each erasedElementId through edit mutation
      Note over IE,Draft: InteractionEngine never mutates DocumentStoreKernel directly.
      Draft->>Touched: record removedElementIds and selectionChanged when removed ids were selected
      Note over Touched: Exact committed scope: removed ids, document, structural, bounds, visual, projection, and selection revision if selection changed.
      IE->>Events: stage deferred erase action descriptor
      Note over Events: Not public yet. Deferred payload is CanvasEraseActionPayload(eraserThickness, erasedElementIds, corridorPointCount).
      EK->>EK: reject Future result before success path
      EK->>CC: compile exact erase touched set and invalidation
      Touched-->>CC: removed ids and revision facts
      CC->>Store: preflight registry, layer membership, and selection invariants
      Store-->>CC: preflight accepted
      CC->>Frame: prepare main repaint masks
      CC->>Events: attach staged erase action to commit
      CC->>Store: install compiled CommitPlan atomically
      Store->>Store: remove registry rows, layer memberships, family rows, and selected ids
      Note over CC,Store: Atomic install is the commit boundary, no action is visible before this point.
      Store->>Spatial: apply touched-id spatial remove for erased ids
      Spatial-->>Store: deleted ids removed from hit and paint indexes
      Store->>Projection: evict public document projection by projectionRevision
      Store->>Events: materialize CanvasActionCommitted erase after install
      Store->>Frame: publish committed main repaint bus
      EK->>EK: close edit session and stale handle
      EK-->>IE: edit result
      IE->>Preview: clear eraser corridor and active session
      Preview->>Frame: request overlay repaint cleanup
      Events->>Signals: publish document revision and erase action notifications
      Frame->>Signals: publish committed main repaint and overlay cleanup repaint notifications
      Signals-->>Surface: repaint main scene without erased elements and overlay without eraser corridor
      IE-->>Tools: terminal handling complete
    end
  end

  opt edit exception, rejected Future, or preflight failure
    EK->>Events: discard pending erase action
    EK->>EK: rollback draft and close session
    EK-->>IE: terminal failure
    IE->>Preview: clear eraser corridor and active session
    Preview->>Frame: request overlay repaint cleanup
    Frame->>Signals: publish overlay cleanup repaint request
    Signals-->>Surface: repaint overlay without eraser corridor
    Note over Store,Signals: Rollback keeps committed document, revisions, selection, spatial index, projection cache, main repaint, public document notifications, and erase action unchanged.
  end
